+---
+id: SPEC-0009
+slug: blast-radius
+schema: keel.spec/1
+status: approved
+scope:
+- src/**
+- test/**
+budget:
+  criteria: 8
+  lines: 200
+---
+
+# blast radius
+
+## Context
+
+`keel serve`'s dashboard fetches `/api/overview` once and polls it, and
+renders a per-feature "Summary" panel from `state.specs` when an operator
+selects a feature in the rail (`assets/ui/app.js`, `renderSpecSummary`). That
+panel shows tiles for runs, tokens, events and open fails, but nothing about
+how much of the codebase the feature's declared scope reaches — the one number
+`src/map/blast.rs` already computes and `keel blast` / `keel plan` already
+print. An operator landing on a feature has no way to see its blast radius
+without leaving the browser for a terminal.
+
+`/api/spec/<slug>` already exists and already narrows `Report::build` to one
+spec, but the JS never calls it — `state.selected` only filters the specs
+already fetched by `/api/overview`. Computing the blast radius inside every
+`SpecReport` built by the unnarrowed `/api/overview` call would recompute the
+whole reverse-import graph, from scratch, for every spec, every 2-second poll
+— the smallest surface is to compute it only for the one spec `/api/spec/<slug>`
+already narrows to, and have the dashboard fetch that route when a feature is
+selected.
+
+## Acceptance criteria
+
+### AC-1 A narrowed report carries the spec's blast radius
+
+WHEN `Report::build` is called with `only` set to one spec's slug and a
+symbol index exists THE SYSTEM SHALL set that spec's `blast` field to an
+object with integer `files`, `lines` and `depth` keys computed by
+`map::blast::compute` over the spec's declared `scope` globs.
+
+oracle: cmd `cargo test --test report the_narrowed_report_carries_the_blast_radius` exit 0
+
+### AC-2 The unnarrowed report stays free of it
+
+WHEN `Report::build` is called with `only` set to `None` THE SYSTEM SHALL
+leave every spec's `blast` field absent, so `/api/overview` does not recompute
+the reverse-import graph once per spec on every poll.
+
+oracle: cmd `cargo test --test report blast_radius_is_absent_from_the_unnarrowed_report` exit 0
+
+### AC-3 A missing symbol index degrades to null
+
+IF the symbol index database does not exist THEN THE SYSTEM SHALL set the
+narrowed spec's `blast` field to `null` rather than making `keel report
+<slug> --json` exit non-zero.
+
+oracle: cmd `cargo test --test report blast_radius_is_null_without_a_symbol_index` exit 0
+
+### AC-4 The depth matches the configured default
+
+THE SYSTEM SHALL compute the narrowed spec's blast radius at
+`cfg.plan.blast_depth`, the same depth `keel blast` and `keel plan` use by
+default, so the number shown on a feature's landing panel and the number
+`keel blast` prints for the same scope agree.
+
+oracle: cmd `cargo test --test report blast_radius_depth_matches_plan_blast_depth` exit 0
+
+### AC-5 `/api/spec/<slug>` serves the field
+
+WHEN a `GET` request reaches `/api/spec/<slug>` for a spec whose scope
+matches at least one indexed file THE SYSTEM SHALL respond with JSON whose
+`specs[0].blast.files` count equals the number of paths `keel blast` reports
+for that spec's scope at the same depth.
+
+oracle: cmd `cargo test --test serve blast_radius_route_matches_keel_blast_output` exit 0
+
+### AC-6 Selecting a feature fetches its blast radius
+
+WHEN the operator selects a feature in the dashboard rail THE SYSTEM SHALL
+fetch `/api/spec/<slug>` for that feature's slug and store the response's
+`blast` field on that feature's state before the Summary panel next renders.
+
+oracle: cmd `cargo test --test serve app_js_fetches_the_spec_route_on_selection` exit 0
+
+### AC-7 The Summary panel shows a blast-radius tile
+
+WHEN the Summary panel renders for a feature whose stored `blast` field is
+not `null` THE SYSTEM SHALL display a tile labelled `blast radius` whose
+value is that field's `files` count.
+
+oracle: cmd `cargo test --test serve app_js_summary_panel_has_a_blast_radius_tile` exit 0
+
+### AC-8 A null blast radius omits the tile
+
+IF a feature's stored `blast` field is `null` THEN THE SYSTEM SHALL omit the
+blast-radius tile from the Summary panel rather than rendering a tile showing
+`0`.
+
+oracle: cmd `cargo test --test serve app_js_omits_the_blast_radius_tile_when_null` exit 0
+
+## Out of scope
+
+- Adding a blast-radius column or tile to the Overview landing view (the
+  `state.selected === null` case) — only a selected feature's own panel.
+- Changing what `map::blast::compute`, `keel blast` or `keel plan` compute;
+  this only surfaces the existing number in `keel serve`.
+- Polling `/api/spec/<slug>` on the same 2-second interval as `/api/overview`;
+  one fetch per selection is all AC-6 requires.
